<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Privacy Policy | BlogHub</title>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Playfair+Display:wght@700&family=Work+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <style>
        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        :root {
            --primary-dark: #1a1a1a;
            --text-primary: #2d2d2d;
            --text-secondary: #666;
            --accent: #d4a373;
            --bg-cream: #faf8f5;
            --border-light: #e5e5e5;
        }

        body {
            font-family: 'Work Sans', sans-serif;
            line-height: 1.7;
            color: var(--text-primary);
            background: var(--bg-cream);
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 80px 24px;
            animation: fadeIn 0.8s ease-out;
        }

        @keyframes fadeIn {
            from {
                opacity: 0;
                transform: translateY(20px);
            }
            to {
                opacity: 1;
                transform: translateY(0);
            }
        }

        header {
            text-align: center;
            margin-bottom: 60px;
            padding-bottom: 40px;
            border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent);
        }

        h1 {
            font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
            font-size: 3.5rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            color: var(--primary-dark);
            margin-bottom: 16px;
            letter-spacing: -0.02em;
            animation: slideDown 0.6s ease-out;
        }

        @keyframes slideDown {
            from {
                opacity: 0;
                transform: translateY(-30px);
            }
            to {
                opacity: 1;
                transform: translateY(0);
            }
        }

        .last-updated {
            font-size: 0.95rem;
            color: var(--text-secondary);
            font-style: italic;
        }

        .intro {
            font-size: 1.15rem;
            color: var(--text-secondary);
            margin-bottom: 48px;
            padding: 24px;
            background: white;
            border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
            border-radius: 4px;
        }

        section {
            margin-bottom: 48px;
            animation: fadeInUp 0.8s ease-out backwards;
        }

        section:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: 0.1s; }
        section:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: 0.15s; }
        section:nth-child(4) { animation-delay: 0.2s; }
        section:nth-child(5) { animation-delay: 0.25s; }
        section:nth-child(6) { animation-delay: 0.3s; }

        @keyframes fadeInUp {
            from {
                opacity: 0;
                transform: translateY(20px);
            }
            to {
                opacity: 1;
                transform: translateY(0);
            }
        }

        h2 {
            font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
            font-size: 2rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            color: var(--primary-dark);
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            padding-top: 20px;
        }

        h2::before {
            content: '';
            display: inline-block;
            width: 40px;
            height: 3px;
            background: var(--accent);
            margin-right: 16px;
            vertical-align: middle;
        }

        h3 {
            font-family: 'Work Sans', sans-serif;
            font-size: 1.25rem;
            font-weight: 600;
            color: var(--primary-dark);
            margin: 24px 0 12px 0;
        }

        p {
            margin-bottom: 16px;
            font-size: 1.05rem;
        }

        ul {
            margin: 20px 0;
            padding-left: 24px;
        }

        li {
            margin-bottom: 12px;
            font-size: 1.05rem;
            line-height: 1.7;
        }

        li::marker {
            color: var(--accent);
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        .highlight {
            background: linear-gradient(180deg, transparent 60%, rgba(212, 163, 115, 0.3) 60%);
            padding: 0 4px;
        }

        .info-box {
            background: white;
            padding: 24px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
            margin: 24px 0;
        }

        .info-box h3 {
            margin-top: 0;
            color: var(--accent);
        }

        .contact-box {
            margin-top: 60px;
            padding: 32px;
            background: white;
            border-radius: 8px;
            border: 1px solid var(--border-light);
            text-align: center;
        }

        .contact-box h3 {
            font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
            font-size: 1.5rem;
            margin-bottom: 12px;
            color: var(--primary-dark);
        }

        .contact-box a {
            color: var(--accent);
            text-decoration: none;
            font-weight: 600;
            border-bottom: 2px solid transparent;
            transition: border-color 0.3s ease;
        }

        .contact-box a:hover {
            border-bottom-color: var(--accent);
        }

        .back-link {
            display: inline-block;
            margin-top: 40px;
            color: var(--text-secondary);
            text-decoration: none;
            font-weight: 500;
            transition: all 0.3s ease;
        }

        .back-link:hover {
            color: var(--accent);
            transform: translateX(-5px);
        }

        .back-link::before {
            content: '← ';
        }

        @media (max-width: 768px) {
            .container {
                padding: 40px 20px;
            }

            h1 {
                font-size: 2.5rem;
            }

            h2 {
                font-size: 1.5rem;
            }

            h2::before {
                width: 30px;
                margin-right: 12px;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <header>
            <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
            <p class="last-updated">Last Updated: January 28, 2026</p>
        </header>

        <div class="intro">
            This Privacy Policy describes how <strong>BlogHub</strong> ("we", "us", or "our") collects, uses, and shares your personal information when you visit or interact with our blog (the "Blog").
        </div>

        <section>
            <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
            
            <h3>1.1 Information You Provide to Us</h3>
            <p>We may collect information that you voluntarily provide to us when you comment on the Blog, subscribe to our newsletter, or contact us. This may include:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Name</li>
                <li>Email address</li>
                <li>Any other information you choose to provide</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>1.2 Information Automatically Collected</h3>
            <p>When you visit our Blog, we automatically collect certain information about your device and browsing activity. This may include:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>IP address</li>
                <li>Browser type and version</li>
                <li>Operating system</li>
                <li>Pages visited and time spent on pages</li>
                <li>Referring website addresses</li>
                <li>Device information</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
            <p>We use the information we collect for various purposes, including to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Provide, maintain, and improve our Blog</li>
                <li>Respond to your comments and questions</li>
                <li>Send you newsletters and marketing communications (if you have opted in)</li>
                <li>Analyze how visitors use our Blog</li>
                <li>Detect, prevent, and address technical issues</li>
                <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>3. Cookies and Tracking Technologies</h2>
            <p>We use cookies and similar tracking technologies to track activity on our Blog and hold certain information. Cookies are files with a small amount of data which may include an anonymous unique identifier.</p>
            
            <div class="info-box">
                <h3>Types of cookies we use:</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Essential cookies:</strong> Required for the Blog to function properly</li>
                    <li><strong>Analytics cookies:</strong> Help us understand how visitors interact with our Blog</li>
                    <li><strong>Preference cookies:</strong> Remember your preferences and settings</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <p>You can instruct your browser to refuse all cookies or to indicate when a cookie is being sent. However, if you do not accept cookies, you may not be able to use some portions of our Blog.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>4. Third-Party Services</h2>
            <p>We may use third-party service providers to analyze the use of our Blog. These third parties may have access to your personal information only to perform these tasks on our behalf and are obligated not to disclose or use it for any other purpose. Examples may include:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Google Analytics for website analytics</li>
                <li>Email service providers for newsletter distribution</li>
                <li>Advertising networks (if applicable)</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>5. Data Retention</h2>
            <p>We will retain your personal information only for as long as is necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Policy. We will retain and use your information to the extent necessary to comply with our legal obligations, resolve disputes, and enforce our policies.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>6. Your Data Protection Rights</h2>
            <p>Depending on your location, you may have the following rights regarding your personal information:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>The right to access:</strong> You have the right to request copies of your personal data</li>
                <li><strong>The right to rectification:</strong> You have the right to request correction of inaccurate information</li>
                <li><strong>The right to erasure:</strong> You have the right to request deletion of your personal data</li>
                <li><strong>The right to restrict processing:</strong> You have the right to request that we restrict processing of your data</li>
                <li><strong>The right to data portability:</strong> You have the right to request transfer of your data</li>
                <li><strong>The right to object:</strong> You have the right to object to our processing of your data</li>
            </ul>
            <p>To exercise any of these rights, please contact us using the information provided below.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>7. Children's Privacy</h2>
            <p>Our Blog is not intended for children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personally identifiable information from children under 13. If you are a parent or guardian and you are aware that your child has provided us with personal information, please contact us so that we can take necessary action.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>8. Security</h2>
            <p>The security of your personal information is important to us, but remember that <span class="highlight">no method of transmission over the Internet or method of electronic storage is 100% secure</span>. While we strive to use commercially acceptable means to protect your personal information, we cannot guarantee its absolute security.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>9. Links to Other Websites</h2>
            <p>Our Blog may contain links to other websites that are not operated by us. If you click on a third-party link, you will be directed to that third party's site. We strongly advise you to review the Privacy Policy of every site you visit. We have no control over and assume no responsibility for the content, privacy policies, or practices of any third-party sites or services.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
            <p>We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page and updating the "Last Updated" date at the top of this Privacy Policy. You are advised to review this Privacy Policy periodically for any changes.</p>
        </section>

        <div class="contact-box">
            <h3>Contact Us</h3>
            <p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us:</p>
            <p>By email: <a href="mailto:contact@bloghub.com">contact@bloghub.com</a></p>
        </div>

        <a href="/" class="back-link">Back to Home</a>
    </div>
</body>
</html>